# Mile to KM Converter

This Python application allows users to convert distances in miles to kilometers. Built with Tkinter, it provides a simple and user-friendly graphical user interface (GUI) to perform the conversion.

## Features

- **User Input**: Allows users to enter the distance in miles.
- **Conversion**: Converts the entered distance from miles to kilometers.
- **Error Handling**: Validates user input and provides feedback for non-numeric input.

## Prerequisites

Before running this application, you must have Python installed on your machine. Python 3.6 or higher is recommended. You can download Python [here](https://www.python.org/downloads/).

## Installation

Clone the repository to your local machine:

```bash
git clone https://github.com/yourusername/mile-to-km-converter.git
cd mile-to-km-converter
```

## Usage

To run the application, execute the following command in the terminal:

```bash
python mile_to_km_converter.py
```

Once the application is running, you can:

1. Enter a numerical value representing miles in the input field.
2. Click on the "Calculate" button to convert the entered distance into kilometers.
3. View the result displayed in the output field below the button.

## How It Works

The application uses the formula:

```
1 Mile = 1.61 Kilometers
```

When you enter the distance in miles and press the "Calculate" button, the application multiplies the entered value by 1.61 to convert it to kilometers and displays the result.
